.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_trace_convergence" "fuzzygene_trace_convergence"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_trace_convergence \- Solver diagnostics of one virtual perturbation, without building the two large matrices.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_trace_convergence(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBgene\fR as string, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockout", 
\fBsteps\fR as integer = 0, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Solver diagnostics of one virtual perturbation, without building the two large matrices.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained (or restored) model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgene\fB \fR\- the target gene of the virtual perturbation. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR (default), \fBknockdown\fR or \fBoverexpression\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsteps\fB \fR\- maximum iteration steps; 0 uses the model configuration. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a named list with \fBconvergence\fR, \fBcontrol_convergence\fR and \fBsummary\fR
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Same solve as \fBfuzzygene_trace_perturbation\fR but only the \fBconvergence\fR /
 \fBcontrol_convergence\fR / \fBsummary\fR elements are returned. Use it when all you need is the
 `log10(max_delta)` versus iteration plot: constructing the 18k x 250 matrices is the
 expensive part.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
